# 4. A simple Java program

```java
public class Hello {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
    }
}
```

Let's break it down.

### Class

```java
public class Hello {
}
```

Java programs are fundamentally organized around **classes and objects**.

### Main method

```java
public static void main(String[] args)
```

This is the traditional entry point for a Java application.

### Output

```java
System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
```

prints text to the console.

