# 9. Java and object-oriented programming

Java became one of the major languages that popularized mainstream OOP.

Its basic object-oriented model includes:

```text
                 Object
                   │
          ┌────────┼────────┐
          ↓        ↓        ↓
       State    Behavior   Identity
```

And major OOP mechanisms:

* encapsulation
* inheritance
* polymorphism
* abstraction
* interfaces
* composition

For example:

```java
interface Animal {
    void speak();
}

class Dog implements Animal {
    @Override
    public void speak() {
        System.out.println("Woof");
    }
}

class Cat implements Animal {
    @Override
    public void speak() {
        System.out.println("Meow");
    }
}
```

Then:

```java
Animal animal = new Dog();
animal.speak();
```

The actual object's implementation is selected at runtime.

This is **runtime polymorphism**.

