# 10. Java's relationship with the Internet

Java became particularly important during the rise of the Internet.

Its history can be viewed roughly like this:

```text
C
│
├── system programming
│
C++
│
├── object-oriented systems programming
│
Java
│
├── portable network/enterprise programming
│
├── server-side applications
│
└── enterprise systems
```

Java's portability, networking APIs, object-oriented model, security model, and large standard library made it attractive for networked applications.

This was especially important in the **late 1990s and 2000s**.

