# 13. Java versus JavaScript

Despite the similar names:

**Java and JavaScript are different languages.**

```text
Java
├── JVM
├── strongly/statically typed
├── class/object oriented
├── enterprise/backend
└── Android historically

JavaScript
├── JavaScript engine
├── dynamically typed
├── web/browser
├── Node.js
└── frontend + backend
```

Historically, the names were related to marketing rather than JavaScript being a version of Java.

---

# 14. Java versus C++

The relationship is more interesting.

Java borrowed many ideas from C and C++ syntax:

```java
if (...)
for (...)
while (...)
class Foo
{
}
```

So Java code can look familiar to a C++ programmer.

But Java deliberately removed or changed several C++ features.

For example, Java doesn't normally have:

* pointer arithmetic
* manual memory management
* multiple class inheritance
* operator overloading
* header files

Instead, Java emphasizes:

```text
automatic memory management
+
interfaces
+
runtime safety
+
portable bytecode
+
managed runtime
```

